"  serve questions [--dir KB]... [--root DIR] [--ledger FILE [--owner KEY]] [--port N]",
"  draft blocking | draft outbound",
"  pin-item ID SOURCE --text-file F --changed-at T [--kind tracker|file]",
"  doctor",
"  help [COMMAND|TOPIC]",
"",
"Finding the KB. orbit-kb uses the first of these:",
"  1. the option --dir DIR;",
"  2. the environment variable ORBIT_KB;",
"  3. the nearest directory, from here upward, with a kb.pl that starts with uses([...]).",
"",
"Exit codes:",
"  0  Success. The query is true. Lint is clean.",
"  1  The query has no answer. Lint found errors. orbit-kb rejected the input.",
"  2  Usage error, missing KB or tool, bad goal, a source that lint must fix first, or SWI ERROR.",
"  A typo never exits 1. Exit 1 always means a real \"no\".",
"",
"Engine:",
"  SWI-Prolog answers every query. Negation is negation as failure: not p holds when p has no answer.",
"  So not under(_) means \"no under at all\". A fact that is not recorded is false.",
"  The rules must be stratified: no predicate depends on itself through not (lint E18).",
"  why and whynot explain a verdict from the same clauses. They never change it.",
"  orbit-kb doctor runs known-answer self-tests.",
"",
"Run orbit-kb help COMMAND for details about one command."
]).

