help_lines(prove, [
"orbit-kb prove CLAIM FILE THEOREM [--module M]",
"",
"Check a Lean proof of a claim, and record it as a lean_proof attestation.",
"FILE is a .lean file in a Lake project. The module is its path, such as Burn/Save.lean -> Burn.Save.",
"orbit-kb runs lake build, reads the theorem, and runs leanchecker. It records the proof only if:",
"  THEOREM is a theorem in the module of FILE;",
"  it depends on no axiom other than propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound (so no sorry and no native_decide);",
"  leanchecker replays the project modules of the proof without a problem.",
"  (It replays only the modules under the project root and outside .lake/. Dependencies are not replayed.)",
"The log runs/proof-ID.log holds the statement and a digest of each file of the proof.",
"It also lists the Lake configuration files that do not exist.",
"If one of these files changes, or an absent one appears, the proof stops counting, and the burn is open again.",
"prove checks the proof of an honest agent that can make mistakes. It does not resist an agent that cheats on purpose.",
"A burn (burn(C)) needs a proof, or a human waiver of the claim (see orbit-kb help attest):",
"  orbit-kb attest waiver c1 \"waive(c1, '2026-11-30T17:00:00Z', 'why')\" --by human",
"A claim that replaces a burning claim (supersedes) burns too, and needs its own proof.",
"orbit-kb cannot check that the statement says what the claim says. Read the statement.",
"Exit 0 when the proof is recorded, 1 when it is not a proof, 2 on a usage error or a missing tool."
]).
help_lines(lint, [
"orbit-kb lint [--strict]",
"",
"Check the KB, the library, and rules.pl. One line per problem, then a summary.",
"E1 syntax. E2 undeclared predicate. E3 type. E4 dangling ref. E5 duplicate id.",
"E6 non-ground fact. E7 clause in the wrong place. E8 writer not allowed. E9 test result or proof without its log.",
"E10 uses/1. E11 a clause does not load. E14 unsafe negation. E17 a form that orbit-kb does not read (s(CASP) syntax).",
"E15 supersede cycle (a claim or hypothesis replaces itself). E16 rules.pl changes done, a burn, flare, waiver, or vote rule, or a computed fact.",
"E18 the rules are not stratified (a predicate depends on itself through not).",
"E19 a predicate declared by its first use has a name 2 edits or fewer from a declared one (a typo?).",
"W1 subject changed. W2 local declaration. W3 claim without cites. W4 local fact that no rule reads.",
"W5 check on a superseded claim, and the new claim has no check yet. W6 local rule that extends a library predicate.",
"W7 a predicate declared by its first use, with who and when. Review it.",
"Module lint_issue/3 results follow. Exit 1 on errors, or on warnings with --strict."
]).
help_lines(query, [
"orbit-kb query 'GOAL' [-n N] [--why] [--long]",
"",
"Answer GOAL.",
"-n N shows N answers. The default is 1. 0 shows all answers.",
"Output: one line per answer, as true or X = v, Y = w. No answer prints false.",
"--why adds, after each answer, the clauses that prove it, 6 levels deep. --long goes 30 levels deep.",
"Exit 0 on an answer, 1 on no answer, 2 on a bad goal, a source that lint must fix first, or SWI ERROR.",
"Discovery vote (D14): 'gate(V)' is the outcome, and has no answer until the human votes.",
"gate_split holds when no other role agrees with the human. 'artifact_vote(V)' is the vote of the formal artifacts."
]).
help_lines(why, [
"orbit-kb why 'GOAL' [-n N] [--long]",
"",
"The same as orbit-kb query --why."
]).
help_lines(whynot, [
"orbit-kb whynot 'GOAL' [--long]",
"",
"The first line is the verdict:",
"  holds    GOAL has an answer. The explanation gives the clauses that prove the first answer.",
"  absent   GOAL has no answer. The explanation gives, for each rule of GOAL, the first literal",
"           that no answer gets past, and why. \"nothing records X\" means that no fact or rule",
"           matches X: the survey can have missed it.",
"The explanation is 6 levels deep; --long goes 30 levels deep. Exit 0."
]).
help_lines(show, [
"orbit-kb show [claims|questions|open|blocking|disclosures|extensions|all]",
"",
"List parts of the KB as plain text. The default is all (all does not include blocking).",
"open lists to_ask, stale, contested, and supersede_cycle, and under, over, burn_open, flare_open, and no_claim (no claim is current) when the build module is in use.",
"blocking lists each answer of orbit-kb query 'blocking(X)' with its text: each item that blocks done.",
"The kinds: to_ask(Q), burn_open(C), flare_open(C), under(C), over(X), check_failing(K), check_unrun(K),",
"waiver_lapsed(W), past_due(X) (an open item with a due/2 time in the past), supersede_cycle(C), no_claim.",
"With the project module: project_conflict(D) and project_kb_unclean (orbit-kb help project)."
]).
help_lines(release, [
"orbit-kb release",
"",
"Free the writer lock of a project KB (orbit-kb help project). Only the holder can release it.",
"With no lock, it does nothing. Exit: 0 on success. 2 when another writer holds the lock."
]).
help_lines(view, [
"orbit-kb view questions [--dir KB]... [--ledger FILE [--owner KEY]] [--out F]",
"",
"Write one HTML page, with no external dependency, of what blocks done in each KB:",
"each question to ask, with its text, its default, the claim it blocks, and the request text",
"that the claim cites, then the other blocking items. Each KB has its own section, named by its",
"pin stamp (spec-kb@sha256:HEX) and labeled with its first request. The options of a question come from the",
"KB's defaults and its option(Q, Text, Effect) facts; each option shows its effect.",
"--dir may repeat. --ledger FILE: a JSON export of the flow ledger; the page lists the asks that",
"wait on the owner (an ask with waits_on null is nobody's), with their age. The owner is --owner KEY,",
"else the owner key in the export, else me. Make the export with: hubflow sql \"SELECT id, kind, title,",
"status, waits_on, age_days, COALESCE((SELECT value FROM meta WHERE key='owner_person'), (SELECT key FROM",
"person WHERE key='me')) AS owner FROM v_open\" --format json > asks.json",
"--out F writes the page to F; without it the page goes to stdout. The view reads only.",
"Exit 2 for a usage error, a KB that cannot be read, or a bad ledger file."
]).
help_lines(serve, [
"orbit-kb serve questions [--dir KB]... [--root DIR] [--ledger FILE [--owner KEY]] [--port N]",
"",
"Serve the page of view questions on http://127.0.0.1:PORT/ (default port 8737; --port 0 picks",
"a free port). Each reload reads the KBs and the ledger again, so the page is live.",
"--dir may repeat. --root DIR serves each kb.pl under DIR. The page groups the spec KBs by the",
"project KB that they name (project_kb), labeled with its first request; a KB with no",
"project_kb is in the group no project. --ledger and --owner work as for view questions; each",
"ask shows the hubflow command that answers it. The page does not answer asks.",
"Each question to ask has a form: its options, other, and a free text. A POST records the",
"answer as answer(Q, Answer, human) with orbit-kb add --by human, and writes nothing else.",
"The write takes the writer lock of the KB (orbit-kb help project) as ORBIT_KB_WRITER, else",
"as human, and gives a lock that was free back after the write. When another writer holds the",
"lock, nothing is written and the page names the holder. The server never uses --take.",
"Safety: it listens on 127.0.0.1 only; a request whose Host is not 127.0.0.1 or localhost gets",
"403; a POST needs the token of this run, which the page carries. There is no login.",
"The server keeps no state of its own. Ctrl-C stops it.",
"Exit 2 for a usage error, a KB that cannot be found, a bad ledger file, or a port in use."
]).
help_lines(pin, [
"orbit-kb pin [--check STAMP]",
"",
"Print the stamp of the KB and the time: spec-kb@sha256:HEX TIME.",
"HEX is the sha256 of kb.pl. orbit-kb computes it. Never type it.",
"Attach the stamp to the ticket, so the ticket names the KB that it relies on.",
"--check STAMP: exit 0 when kb.pl still has that digest, and 1 when it changed.",
"The whole line of pin is a valid STAMP. A malformed STAMP is a usage error (exit 2).",
"pin writes nothing."
]).
help_lines(draft, [
"orbit-kb draft blocking",
"orbit-kb --dir PROJECT draft outbound",
"",
"Drafts only: nothing is sent to a tracker, and no command uses a network.",
"draft blocking prints Markdown: the stamp spec-kb@sha256:HEX of kb.pl, then each item that",
"blocks done, as show blocking does. Paste it into the ticket. orbit-kb pin --check STAMP",
"exits 1 once kb.pl has changed. It writes nothing.",
"draft outbound lists the project KB drafts that are not pushed (needs the project module).",
"It reads only the KB it runs in, so give the project KB: orbit-kb --dir PROJECT draft outbound."
]).
help_lines('pin-item', [
"orbit-kb --dir PROJECT pin-item ID SOURCE --text-file F --changed-at T [--kind tracker|file]",
"",
"Record a pin of a tracker item in a project KB, from item text that you pasted or exported",
"into the file F. orbit-kb computes the digest (sha256 of F). You give the change time",
"(--changed-at, UTC, such as 2026-10-01T09:00:00Z). --kind defaults to tracker.",
"It writes pin/5, so it takes the writer lock and accepts --take (D23). A pin id that exists",
"is rejected (exit 1). Nothing is fetched: no command uses a network."
]).
help_lines(report, [
"orbit-kb report [--html FILE [--open]]",
"",
"Print a delivery report skeleton with these sections:",
"Delivered, Claims, Guesses, Disclosures, Waivers (build), Not checked, Open, To land.",
"With the discovery module, a Vote section comes before To land. It shows the agent's vote",
"and the formal artifacts' vote only after the human votes in the current round.",
"Fill in Delivered and To land yourself.",
"",
"The text is plain Markdown. Each section has a heading (# Claims:) and a blank line after it.",
"Each item is a bullet, with two more spaces for each level. The label is in **bold**.",
"A claim that needs attention (under, a waiver, a burn that is not proved, a flare, a check that did not",
"pass) puts its status, burn, flare, and checks in nested bullets. A fulfilled claim with nothing to add",
"stays on one line, when the line fits in 100 columns. Long lines are not wrapped.",
"",
"--html FILE also writes the report as one page for a human to review in a browser.",
"The text on stdout does not change. The page works offline. It shows the open items first,",
"then each claim with its status, its checks (latest run and log), and its evidence.",
"The reviewer marks items ok, doubt, or wrong, with a note, and copies the marks as text",
"to paste back to you, such as: c1: doubt - the example does not cover X.",
"--open opens the page with xdg-open (or open). Without --open, nothing opens."
]).
help_lines(doctor, [
"orbit-kb doctor",
"",
"Check swipl and the library. Then run known-answer self-tests on the engine, as a query runs:",
"not with a helper rule, and not under(_), are false when under(a) holds;",
"arithmetic under not gives exactly k2, k3, k4;",
"E18 flags p :- not q, q :- not p; E17 flags -p(b).",
"Exit 2 if something is missing or a self-test fails."
]).
